On a related note, one thing that seems to be missing from the usual
spoilers is an indication of which corpses convey poison resistance
but aren't *themselves* poisonous.

SPOILERS follow, obviously...










I believe a "safe" list of corpses conveying poison resistance is:

        quivering blobs, pyrolisks, quasits, blue jellies, cave
        spiders, centipedes, all unicorns, brown molds, red molds,
        shriekers, red/golden/guardian naga hatchlings, red/golden
        nagas, flesh golems

Also nearly safe are these corpses, though you might take up to 15
points of acid indigestion damage from eating them:

        black nagas and their hatchlings, gray oozes, brown and black
        puddings

Note that giant spiders and grown-up guardian nagas *are* poisonous.

Additionally, these corpses can convey poison resistance, but have
other disadvantages:

        violet fungi - cause hallucination
        tengus - can convey teleportitis (but also teleport ctrl)
        nurses - could make you a cannibal

In theory, chickatrices and cockatrices could convey poison resistance
without poisoning you, but only if you're polymorphed into something
stoning resistant.  Also, the Wizard of Yendor and Master Kaen convey
poison resistance, too, if you manage to make it that far without
otherwise getting the resistance and can take the cannibalism hit
where it applies.

